{title: Do Not Be Anxious}
{subtitle: Philippians 4:6–7}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm7] | [Cm7] | [F7] | [Bbmaj7] |
| [G7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cm7]Late at night my mind won't [F7]rest
Running through the what ifs [Bbmaj7]
[Cm7]Lay it down, the weight I [F7]hold
Everything in prayer [Bbmaj7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Do not be anx[Cm7]ious about a[F7]nything
[Bbmaj7]Bring it all to God with [G7]thanks
And the peace [Cm7]that passes un[F7]derstanding
[Bbmaj7]Will guard your heart and [G7]mind
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [G7] | [Cm7] | [F7] | [Bbmaj7] |
| [Bbmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm7]Every worry, every fear
[F7]Every little thing [Bbmaj7]
[Cm7]Say it slowly, say thank [F7]you
Let it go to him [Bbmaj7]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [G7] | [Cm7] | [F7] | [Bbmaj7] |
| [G7] | [G7] |
